    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks. that makes sense. one thing though, i noticed when the turbo starts spooling up it makes a really distinct high-pitched whistling or whining sound. is there a mechanical reason why it makes that specific noise during the boost phase?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "That high-pitched whine is primarily caused by air vibrating through the narrow gaps between the spinning compressor blades and the compressor housing walls as the speed increases. Additionally, turbulence at the junction where the exhaust gases enter the turbine can generate whistling frequencies that become more prominent as the device spools up. In isolation, these two aerodynamic and mechanical vibrations create the distinct sound you hear during the boost phase.",
